@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:5000
@antiforgeryToken = REPLACE_FROM_EMAIL_TEST_FORM
@testEmail = REPLACE_WITH_ALLOWLISTED_SYNTHETIC_INBOX
@testPassword = REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_TEST_PASSWORD
@challengeId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@verificationToken = REPLACE_FROM_VERIFICATION_EMAIL
@loginCode = REPLACE_FROM_LOGIN_EMAIL

### Open the browser form first. Retain its antiforgery cookie and copy the form token.
GET {{baseUrl}}/email-test

### Register synthetic learner. An unallowlisted address is rejected.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email-test/register
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

email={{testEmail}}&password={{testPassword}}&confirmPassword={{testPassword}}&__RequestVerificationToken={{antiforgeryToken}}

### Confirm a verification link. Reused, expired, and invalid tokens are rejected.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email-test/verify
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

id={{challengeId}}&token={{verificationToken}}&__RequestVerificationToken={{antiforgeryToken}}

### Password step creates a pending cookie, not an authentication cookie.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

email={{testEmail}}&password={{testPassword}}&returnUrl=%2Femail-test

### Retain the pending cookie and refresh the antiforgery token from the code form.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email-test/code
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

code={{loginCode}}&__RequestVerificationToken={{antiforgeryToken}}

### Requires test-learner authentication and a current form antiforgery token.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email-test/certificate
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

__RequestVerificationToken={{antiforgeryToken}}

### Anonymous requests redirect to login; other users cannot download this sample.
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/email-test/certificate

### Open state-first roster selection in the browser.
GET {{baseUrl}}/roster-registration

### Register a new allowlisted test inbox with a local pending roster association.
### Replace the record ID with a selection from the latest approved snapshot.
@licenseeId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email-test/roster-register
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

licenseeId={{licenseeId}}&email={{testEmail}}&password={{testPassword}}&confirmPassword={{testPassword}}&__RequestVerificationToken={{antiforgeryToken}}

### Existing test learner: requires signed-in, verified email and a current form token.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email-test/roster-submit
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

licenseeId={{licenseeId}}&__RequestVerificationToken={{antiforgeryToken}}
